  {# ── THE IDEA ── #}
  <section class="bg-white px-6 py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6 text-lg/8 text-night-bordeaux-500">
      <h2 class="font-heading text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-blazing-flame-500">Bringing families back to the work site</h2>
      <p>
        Some corporations invest in a daycare on site, so parents can visit their kids during the day and see them
        grow. Family Cooperative Work Sites asks how that idea can reach everyone, with safety and
        proximity both achieved.
      </p>
      <p>
        Imagine someone doing blue-collar work taking a break and spending it with their own children.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {# ── HISTORY ── #}
  <section class="bg-cotton-candy-100 px-6 py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6 text-lg/8 text-night-bordeaux-500">
      <h2 class="font-heading text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-seagrass-700">Work and home used to share a roof</h2>
      <p>
        For most of human history, work and family lived side by side. Farms, workshops and shops were
        run by households, and children grew up watching and joining in the work. The factory, the office
        and the commute pulled the two apart. Family Cooperative Work Sites are about weaving them
        back together, in a way that suits today's work.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

